:: Start [nobar]
<<include "Banner">>
<div class="stamp">Case file 002</div>
<p class="meta">U.S. Marshals Service · San Francisco · today</p>
<h1>The Marshals' File</h1>
<p>It's your first week as a deputy U.S. Marshal. Your boss drops a thick, faded folder on your desk. The label says <b>MORRIS, ANGLIN, ANGLIN — ESCAPE, JUNE 11, 1962</b>.</p>
<p class="quote chief">"Oldest open file in the office. The FBI closed theirs in 1979 and said they drowned. We never closed ours. Go through it, decide what you think happened, and tell me whether we keep it open. Seven leads."</p>
<<if $fromLocker>><div class="card"><span class="card-label">From your evidence locker</span><span class="card-title">Allen West's statement</span><span class="card-text">You bagged this in Part 1. It's already in your notebook.</span></div><</if>>
<div class="how">
<p><b>How to investigate</b></p>
<ul>
<li>Visiting a new place uses one lead. Going back is free.</li>
<li>Interviews: two questions each.</li>
<li>Some clues are <b>tested facts</b>. Some are <b>claims</b> nobody can check. Some are <b>expert opinions</b>. Before your verdict, you'll sort them.</li>
<li><b>This case has no answer key.</b> "We can't tell yet" is a real verdict if your evidence points both ways.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="actions">[[Open the file|Hub]]</div>


:: Hub
<<if $leads lte 0>><<goto "OutOfLeads">><</if>>
<<set _ev to setup.events.filter(function(e){ return $leads <= e.at && !$events.includes(e.id); })>>
<<for _e range _ev>><<run $events.push(_e.id)>>
<<if _e.kind is "headline">><div class="headline"><span class="paper">News alert</span><<print _e.text>></div>
<<else>><p class="quote chief"><<print _e.text>></p><</if>>
<</for>>
<h2>Where to?</h2>
<p class="meta">New places cost a lead. Places you've visited are free to revisit.</p>
<<casemap>>
<details class="maplist"><summary>Show the places as a list</summary>
<ul class="map">
<li><<maplink "Search" "🛶 The 1962 search reports">></li>
<li><<maplink "WestFile" "📄 Allen West's statement">></li>
<li><<maplink "Bay" "⚓ The Coast Guard station: the bay itself">></li>
<li><<maplink "Memo" "📁 The FBI's 1979 closing memo">></li>
<li><<maplink "Widner" "🗣️ Interview David Widner, the Anglins' nephew">></li>
<li><<maplink "Roderick" "⭐ Interview Art Roderick, retired marshal">></li>
<li><<maplink "Lab" "🔬 The FBI lab report on the 2013 letter">></li>
<li><<maplink "Hut" "💻 Video call with Rolf Hut, tide scientist">></li>
<li><<maplink "Tests" "🎬 The raft tests: video archive">></li>
<li><<maplink "Newsroom" "📰 A newsroom">></li>
</ul>
</details>
<div class="actions secondary"><<link "Deduction board (free)">><<set $return to "Hub">><<goto "Board">><</link>>[[I'm ready to decide|Sort]]</div>


:: OutOfLeads
<h2>Out of leads</h2>
<p class="quote chief">"That's enough digging," your boss says. "What's your call?"</p>
<div class="actions"><<link "One last look at the deduction board">><<set $return to "OutOfLeads">><<goto "Board">><</link>>[[Make your call|Sort]]</div>


:: Search
<h2>The 1962 search reports</h2>
<<include "Scene">>
<p>Yellowed typed pages, maps of the bay with pencil circles, and photos of soggy objects laid out on a table.</p>
<<clue "paddle">>
<<clue "packet">>
<<clue "vests">>
<<clue "nobodies">>
<<tomap>>


:: WestFile
<h2>Allen West's statement</h2>
<p>The fourth man, the one whose vent jammed, told investigators everything he knew.</p>
<<clue "west">>
<<tomap>>


:: Bay
<h2>The Coast Guard station</h2>
<p>From the window you can see Alcatraz out in the bay, and the Golden Gate Bridge beyond it. A Coast Guard officer pulls up the records.</p>
<<clue "cold">>
<<clue "scott">>
<<tomap>>


:: Memo
<h2>The FBI's 1979 closing memo</h2>
<p>Seventeen years of work, ending in a few pages.</p>
<<clue "fbi79">>
<<clue "nothefts">>
<p>Clipped to the back: a newer Marshals Service note.</p>
<<clue "rule99">>
<<tomap>>


:: Widner
<h2>Interview: David Widner</h2>
<p>David Widner is the Anglin brothers' nephew. His family has spent years trying to prove his uncles made it.</p>
<div id="ans"><<pastanswers "widner">></div>
<div id="iv"><<interview "widner">></div>
<<tomap>>


:: Roderick
<h2>Interview: Art Roderick</h2>
<p>Art Roderick worked the Alcatraz case for the Marshals for about twenty years before he retired.</p>
<div id="ans"><<pastanswers "roderick">></div>
<div id="iv"><<interview "roderick">></div>
<<tomap>>


:: Lab
<h2>The FBI lab report</h2>
<p>A photocopy of the 2013 letter, with the lab's report clipped to the front.</p>
<<clue "letter">>
<<clue "lettertest">>
<<tomap>>


:: Hut
<h2>Video call: Rolf Hut</h2>
<p>Rolf Hut is a scientist at Delft University in the Netherlands. In 2014, his team built a computer model of San Francisco Bay's tides, then sent pretend rafts through it to see where they'd end up.</p>
<div id="ans"><<pastanswers "hut">></div>
<div id="iv"><<interview "hut">></div>
<<tomap>>


:: Tests
<h2>The raft tests</h2>
<p>A stack of videos, from 2003 to 2025, of people trying to cross the bay the way the escapers did.</p>
<<clue "mythbusters">>
<<clue "rober">>
<<clue "aged">>
<<tomap>>


:: Newsroom
<h2>A newsroom</h2>
<p>Every anniversary, the Alcatraz story comes back.</p>
<p class="quote">"They're on a beach in Brazil right now," says one reporter. "Bet someone had a boat waiting," says another.</p>
<<clue "brazilbeach">>
<<clue "guard">>
<<tomap>>


:: Sort [nobar]
<<set _pool to setup.sortOrder.filter(function(id){ return $notebook.includes(id); }).slice(0, 6)>>
<<set $sortTotal to _pool.length>>
<div class="stamp">Sort the evidence</div>
<h2>Fact, claim, or opinion?</h2>
<p>Before you decide, sort your key evidence. A <b>tested fact</b> is something that was checked or measured. A <b>claim</b> is something someone says, which nobody has been able to check. An <b>expert opinion</b> is what an expert concludes from the evidence.</p>
<<if _pool.length is 0>><p class="note">You don't have any key evidence to sort. You'll go straight to your verdict.</p>
<<else>><div id="sortlist"><<include "SortList">></div><</if>>
<div class="actions">[[On to my verdict|Accusation]]</div>


:: SortList
<<set _pool to setup.sortOrder.filter(function(id){ return $notebook.includes(id); }).slice(0, 6)>>
<<for _id range _pool>><<capture _id>>
<div class="sortrow"><p class="card-title"><<print setup.cards[_id].title>></p><p class="card-text"><<print setup.cards[_id].text>></p>
<div class="choices three"><<for _k range ["fact","claim","opinion"]>><<capture _k>><span @class="$sort[_id] is _k ? 'opt chosen' : 'opt'"><<link setup.kindLabel[_k]>><<set $sort[_id] to _k>><<replace "#sortlist">><<include "SortList">><</replace>><</link>></span><</capture>><</for>></div></div>
<</capture>><</for>>
<p class="meta">Sorted: <<print _pool.filter(function(id){ return $sort[id]; }).length>> of <<print _pool.length>></p>


:: Accusation [nobar]
<div class="stamp">Verdict</div>
<h2>"So, did they make it?"</h2>
<p class="quote chief">"Your verdict, how sure you are, up to three cards that back it up, and what we do with the file."</p>
<h3>1. Your verdict</h3>
<div id="verdicts"><<include "VerdictList">></div>
<h3>2. How sure are you?</h3>
<div id="confs"><<include "ConfList">></div>
<h3>3. Pin up to 3 cards as evidence</h3>
<<if $notebook.length is 0>><p class="note">Your notebook is empty. You'll have to report with no evidence.</p>
<<else>><div id="pins"><<include "PinList">></div><</if>>
<h3>4. The file: keep it open, or close it?</h3>
<div id="decs"><<include "DecisionList">></div>
<div id="file"><<include "FileButton">></div>


:: VerdictList
<<set _opts to [["made","They made it"],["drowned","They drowned"],["unknown","We can't tell yet"]]>>
<div class="choices"><<for _o range _opts>><<capture _o>><span @class="$verdict is _o[0] ? 'opt chosen' : 'opt'"><<link _o[1]>><<set $verdict to _o[0]>><<replace "#verdicts">><<include "VerdictList">><</replace>><<replace "#file">><<include "FileButton">><</replace>><</link>></span><</capture>><</for>></div>


:: ConfList
<<set _opts to [["hunch","Just a hunch"],["fairly","Fairly sure"],["very","Very sure"]]>>
<div class="choices"><<for _o range _opts>><<capture _o>><span @class="$conf is _o[0] ? 'opt chosen' : 'opt'"><<link _o[1]>><<set $conf to _o[0]>><<replace "#confs">><<include "ConfList">><</replace>><<replace "#file">><<include "FileButton">><</replace>><</link>></span><</capture>><</for>></div>


:: PinList
<p class="meta">Pinned: <<print $pinned.length>> of 3. Tap a card to pin or unpin it.</p>
<div class="cards pinboard">
<<for _id range $notebook>><<capture _id>><span @class="($pinned.includes(_id) ? 'opt pinned' : 'opt') + (setup.cards[_id].type === 'deduction' ? ' ded' : '')"><<link setup.cards[_id].title>><<if $pinned.includes(_id)>><<run $pinned.delete(_id)>><<elseif $pinned.length lt 3>><<run $pinned.push(_id)>><</if>><<replace "#pins">><<include "PinList">><</replace>><</link>></span><</capture>><</for>>
</div>


:: DecisionList
<<set _opts to [["openBodies","Keep it open: no bodies were found, so nobody has proven they died"],["openLetter","Keep it open: the letter proves they made it"],["closeAge","Close it: they'd be about 100, the age when the Marshals stop hunting"],["closeRaft","Close it: a raincoat raft could never cross the bay"]]>>
<div class="choices"><<for _o range _opts>><<capture _o>><span @class="$decision is _o[0] ? 'opt chosen' : 'opt'"><<link _o[1]>><<set $decision to _o[0]>><<replace "#decs">><<include "DecisionList">><</replace>><<replace "#file">><<include "FileButton">><</replace>><</link>></span><</capture>><</for>></div>


:: FileButton
<<if $verdict is "" or $conf is "" or $decision is "">><p class="note">Choose a verdict, how sure you are, and what to do with the file.</p>
<<else>><div class="actions">[[File my decision|Verdict]]</div><</if>>


:: Verdict [nobar]
<<set _pool to setup.sortOrder.filter(function(id){ return $notebook.includes(id); }).slice(0, 6)>>
<<set $sortRight to _pool.filter(function(id){ return $sort[id] === setup.cards[id].type; }).length>>
<<set _pinLean to $pinned.map(function(id){ return setup.cards[id].lean; })>>
<<set _nM to _pinLean.filter(function(x){ return x === "made"; }).length>>
<<set _nD to _pinLean.filter(function(x){ return x === "drowned"; }).length>>
<<set _nG to $pinned.filter(function(id){ return setup.cards[id].type === "assumption"; }).length>>
<<set _hasFact to $pinned.some(function(id){ return setup.cards[id].type === "fact"; })>>
<<if $verdict is "made">><<set _s1 to _nM gte 2 and _nG is 0 and _hasFact>>
<<elseif $verdict is "drowned">><<set _s1 to _nD gte 2 and _nG is 0 and _hasFact>>
<<else>><<set _s1 to _nM gte 1 and _nD gte 1 and _nG is 0>><</if>>
<<if $verdict is "unknown">><<set _s2 to $conf isnot "very">>
<<elseif $conf is "very">><<set _s2 to false>>
<<elseif $conf is "fairly">><<set _s2 to _s1>>
<<else>><<set _s2 to true>><</if>>
<<set _s3 to _pool.length gte 3 and $sortRight gte _pool.length - 1>>
<<set _s4 to ($decision is "openBodies" and $notebook.includes("nobodies")) or ($decision is "closeAge" and $notebook.includes("rule99"))>>
<<set $stars to (_s1 ? 1 : 0) + (_s2 ? 1 : 0) + (_s3 ? 1 : 0) + (_s4 ? 1 : 0)>>
<<set $deductions to $notebook.filter(function(id){ return setup.cards[id].type === "deduction"; }).length>>
<<switch $verdict>>
<<case "made">><div class="stamp">Verdict: made it</div>
<<case "drowned">><div class="stamp">Verdict: drowned</div>
<<default>><div class="stamp solved">Verdict: can't tell yet</div>
<</switch>>
<h2>Detective rating: <<print $stars>> of 4 stars</h2>
<p class="meta">Nobody knows the true answer, so these stars measure how well you used evidence, not whether you "won."</p>
<ul class="stars">
<li @class="_s1 ? 'on' : 'off'"><span aria-hidden="true"><<print _s1 ? '★' : '☆'>></span> <b>Evidence that fits your verdict.</b> <<if _s1>>The cards you pinned back up what you said<<if $verdict isnot "unknown">>, and at least one is a tested fact<</if>>.<<elseif _nG gt 0>>You pinned a reporter's guess. Guesses aren't evidence.<<elseif $verdict is "unknown">>For "can't tell yet," pin at least one card pointing each way.<<elseif not _hasFact>>Claims and opinions alone aren't enough. Pin at least one tested fact.<<else>>Pin at least two cards that point toward your verdict.<</if>></li>
<li @class="_s2 ? 'on' : 'off'"><span aria-hidden="true"><<print _s2 ? '★' : '☆'>></span> <b>Confidence that fits the evidence.</b> <<if $conf is "very" and $verdict isnot "unknown">>The evidence points both ways, so "very sure" is too sure.<<elseif $verdict is "unknown" and $conf is "very">>Very sure that nobody can tell? Fair, but "fairly sure" fits better.<<elseif _s2>>Your confidence matches how strong your evidence is.<<else>>"Fairly sure" needs pinned evidence that backs you up. Otherwise it's a hunch.<</if>></li>
<li @class="_s3 ? 'on' : 'off'"><span aria-hidden="true"><<print _s3 ? '★' : '☆'>></span> <b>Facts, claims and opinions.</b> <<if _pool.length lt 3>>You didn't collect enough key evidence to sort.<<else>>You sorted <<print $sortRight>> of <<print _pool.length>> correctly.<<if not _s3>> Ask: did anyone test it, or is it just someone's word?<</if>><</if>></li>
<li @class="_s4 ? 'on' : 'off'"><span aria-hidden="true"><<print _s4 ? '★' : '☆'>></span> <b>A file decision backed by evidence.</b> <<switch $decision>><<case "openBodies">><<if _s4>>No bodies means nobody has proven they died. A fair reason to keep looking.<<else>>Fair reason, but you never read the search reports that show it.<</if>><<case "closeAge">><<if _s4>>They'd be about 100, the age when the Marshals stop hunting. A fair reason to close it.<<else>>Fair reason, but you never found out how long the Marshals hunt.<</if>><<case "openLetter">>The letter is a claim the lab couldn't prove. It can't prove anything by itself.<<default>>Three different tests showed a raft could cross. "Could never" isn't true.<</switch>></li>
</ul>
<p class="meta">Deductions worked out: <<print $deductions>> of <<print setup.dedTotal>></p>
<h3>Your notebook, flipped over</h3>
<<if $notebook.length is 0>><p class="note">You didn't collect any cards.</p><<else>>
<div class="cards reveal"><<for _id range $notebook>><<set _c to setup.cards[_id]>><div @class="'card ' + (_c.type === 'deduction' ? 'deduction' : _c.lean)"><span class="tag"><<print setup.kindLabel[_c.type]>><<if _c.type isnot "assumption" and _c.type isnot "deduction">> · <<print setup.leanLabel[_c.lean]>><</if>></span><span class="card-title"><<print _c.title>></span><<if $pinned.includes(_id)>><span class="pinned-mark">You pinned this</span><</if>></div><</for>></div><</if>>
<div class="actions">[[What's known today|RealHistory]]</div>


:: RealHistory [nobar]
<h2>What's known today</h2>
<p>The FBI still thinks the three men most likely drowned. The Marshals kept the case open for decades, and in 2022 they released computer-made pictures of how the men might look in old age.</p>
<p>The family still believes they made it. The photo and the letter have never been proven real or fake. The raft tests show the crossing was possible on the right tide. No body, no grave and no confirmed sighting has ever been found.</p>
<p>Frank Morris would have turned 100 on September 1, 2026. When this game was made, in October 2026, we couldn't find any public announcement about the case.</p>
<div class="lesson">
<h3>Your lesson as a trainee</h3>
<ul>
<li>Possible is not the same as proven.</li>
<li>A test anyone can repeat is stronger than a claim nobody can check.</li>
<li>"We can't tell yet" is an honest answer, not a failure.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<p class="note">David Widner, Art Roderick and Rolf Hut are real people. Their interview answers are written for this game, based on what they told reporters. Your boss and the reporters are made up.</p>
<div class="actions">[[Finish case|CaseClosed]]</div>


:: CaseClosed [nobar]
<<include "Banner">>
<<run setup.reportResult()>>
<div class="stamp solved big">Case closed</div>
<h2>Case 002, Part 2 complete</h2>
<p>Detective rating: <b><<print $stars>> of 4</b>. Deductions: <b><<print $deductions>> of <<print setup.dedTotal>></b>.</p>
<p>Tell Rocky your verdict, how sure you were, and whether you kept the file open.</p>
<div class="actions secondary"><<link "Play again">><<run Engine.restart()>><</link>></div>


